# Residential Swimming Pool, Deck, Seating Zone & Restroom/Steam Room Block

A complete pre-construction planning package for a residential swimming pool project in Bengaluru, India — covering design layout, quantity takeoff, tier-wise cost estimation, and a 42-task construction schedule from mobilization to handover.

This repository showcases an end-to-end civil/project-engineering workflow: reading architectural drawings, extracting real quantities, building a market-grounded cost model, and sequencing the build into a working project schedule.

---

## Project Scope

The project covers four functional zones on a single plot (20' × 60'-0.5"):

| Zone | Size | Contents |
|---|---|---|
| Restroom / Steam Block | 17' × 18'-5.5" (314 sqft) | Men's & Women's shower rooms, Men's & Women's restrooms, Steam room, side passages |
| Seating Zone | 20' × 5'-7" (112 sqft) | Umbrella seating area between the restroom block and the pool deck |
| Swimming Pool | 11'-1.5" × 33'-0.5", 5'-6" uniform depth | Sun shelf & step entry, full-length swim zone |
| Deck / Walkway | 4'-11" wide | Runs the length of the pool, with loungers on the opposite edge and landscaping at the far end |

---

## Repository Contents

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `Pool_Design_Rendered_Layout.pdf` | Top-down illustrative rendering of the layout, drawn to scale from the floor plan and dimension drawings |
| `Pool_Construction_Schedule.pdf` | 42-task project schedule (Mobilization → Handover), Mon–Sat working week |
| `Pool_Costing_RateAnalysis.pdf` | Tier-wise (Normal / Modern / Premium / Luxury) rate analysis, quantity takeoff, and Bengaluru market-rate basis |

---

## Design & Layout

Quantities were taken off directly from the floor plan and dimension drawings rather than assumed:

- **Pool water surface:** 350 sqft (floor) + 486 sqft (walls, at confirmed 5'-6" depth) = **836 sqft total wetted area**
- **Pool coping run:** ~27 running metres
- **Pool shell concrete volume:** ~12 cum (150mm wall + floor thickness)
- **Restroom block built-up area:** 314 sqft
- **Deck area (net):** 368 sqft

See `Pool_Design_Rendered_Layout.pdf` for the scaled visual layout.

---

## Project Schedule

- **Start:** 25-May-2026
- **Finish:** 07-Aug-2026
- **Duration:** 75 calendar days
- **Working week:** Monday–Saturday (Sunday off)
- **42 tasks** across 7 phases:
  1. Pre-Construction
  2. Earthwork & Excavation
  3. Structural Work
  4. MEP Rough-In
  5. Waterproofing & Plastering
  6. Tiling & Finishing
  7. Grouting, Testing & Handover

Each task carries duration, predecessor logic, and calculated start/end dates — compatible for import into MS Project, Primavera P6, or SAP PS.

---

## Cost Estimation

A phase-wise rate analysis was built across four finish tiers, using **Premium as the baseline specification** (branded fittings, quality tiles/coping, standard imported-grade filtration):

| Tier | Multiplier vs. Premium | Grand Total (₹, incl. 5% contingency + 18% GST) |
|---|---|---|
| Normal | ≈ 0.50× | ₹26.3 lakh |
| Modern | ≈ 0.75× | ₹39.5 lakh |
| **Premium (baseline)** | 1.00× | ₹52.8 lakh |
| Luxury | ≈ 1.75× | ₹92.3 lakh |

Rates are grounded in 2026 Bengaluru market data (RCC pool construction, waterproofing, filtration/MEP, tiling & coping benchmarks) — see the `Market Basis` tab in the workbook for sourcing detail.

*Figures are indicative for budgeting purposes only; obtain contractor quotes before finalizing.*

---

## Methodology

1. **Design intake** — floor plan and dimension drawings reviewed to extract real measurements
2. **Quantity takeoff** — areas, volumes, and running lengths calculated per work item (documented in the `Quantity Takeoff` tab)
3. **Rate analysis** — unit rates researched and applied across four finish tiers
4. **Scheduling** — 42-task dependency-linked schedule built on a Mon–Sat working calendar
5. **Rendering** — scaled top-down layout produced for visual reference

---

## Tools Used

Excel (rate analysis & scheduling), PDF drawings, SVG-based scaled rendering.

